<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> a prov:SoftwareAgent;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "delphisci dataset-resolvability assessor (Grok 4.7)";
    prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/usesModel> <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7-high-fast>.
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7-high-fast> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LanguageModel>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7";
    dc:identifier "grok-4.7-high-fast".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2018-hcn2-11--grok> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7 on levin-2018-hcn2-11: needs-new-data, resolvability 0.38";
    dc:description "The three percentages and the indistinguishability claim are a straightforward contingency-table test. Those counts were not deposited, and the data statement does not point to a repository. Re-reading Figure 5f repeats the claim rather than testing it. The design would discriminate rescue from a partial improvement once the individual outcomes exist.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: Count major brain-morphology defects at stage 45 in untreated controls, nicotine (0.1 mg/mL, stages 10–35), and nicotine plus Hcn2-WT mRNA. Rescue to control levels is confirmed if nicotine is near 60% and the HCN2 arm is statistically indistinguishable from the ~7% control; a residual elevation in the HCN2 arm would refute complete rescue.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Injection and nicotine timing have to match the stated window.", "Major-defect categories can be scored differently by another observer.", "The bar graph is not accompanied by an open embryo-level table.";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasConfidence> "0.75"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasScore> "0.381"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasVerdict> "needs-new-data".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/levin-2018-hcn2-11--grok--analysis-feasibility> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Analysis feasibility of levin-2018-hcn2-11 by Grok 4.7: 0.18";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.2.0-analysis-feasibility>;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.2.0/analysis-feasibility";
